On 31 May 2006 10:54:54 -0700, Doug Freyburger wrote:

>Jakob Creutzig wrote:
>> Getsome writes:
>>
>> > I got a samarai and am trying to figure out how to #twoweapon
>> > every time I try I end up wielding my pickax or I am left empty handed
>> > how do I do it?
>>
>> Nethack has a "wielded weapon" and an "alternate weapon" slot.  So,
>>
>> 1) Wield weapon #1.
>> 2) Type 'x' for moving #1 to "alternate" slot.
>> 3) Wield weapon #2.
>> 4) Type #twoweapon.
>
>Note that when you #twoweapon the artifact has to be the one
>in the primary slot not the alternate slot.  Use "x" again to put
>it there.  Also in vanilla it doesn't work with two artifacts.  They
>refuse to play second fiddle even to better artifacts.

  Something that may help is #adjust secondary weapon to 'x' and primary
weapon to 'w'.  Then 'wxx' to set the secondary weapon. 'ww' to set the
primary weapon.  Then "#twoweapon".  Might be worth trying to set that
up in the paste buffer: "wxxww#twoweapon".


>
>And something that doesn't apply to samurai - Not all classes
>are able to #twoweapon.

  As with almost everything in NetHack, this is only sort of true.
Polymorphing into some monsters permits twoweaponing for any class.
Marilith is one, I believe.

  Of course, unskilled twoweaponing gives -9 to hit and -3 damage bonus
per hit.  This also applies to all #twoweaponing classes when they start
twoweaponing.  Twoweaponing uses the lower of weapon skill and twoweapon
skill for each weapon.



